      "level": 1,
      "content": "Insert Element to an Empty Linked List"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Before inserting a node in a linked list we must first check if the linked list is empty or not."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If you recall the LinkedList class we introduced in the previous lesson, its head is initially set to nullptr."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "// Initialize head to nullptr\nLinkedList(): head(nullptr){}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This means that the head of an empty linked list is nullptr."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Therefore, to add a new node to an empty linked list, we just need to make the head point to the new node"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "// Check if the linked list is empty\nif (head == nullptr){\n    // Set the new node as the head\n    head = new_node;\n}"
    },
